    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47436" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tămăsŏs</span></b> ,
		i, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τάμασος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an ancient city of
				Cyprus</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 31, 35, §
			130</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tămăsēus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Tamasus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 644</span></i>
			.</div>
